<p>U.S. military forces boarded and seized a sanctioned oil tanker in the Indian Ocean — the third such interdiction in that region — the Pentagon said on Tuesday. The seizure comes as the U.S. steps up pressure on vessels moving oil to and from Venezuela, following a U.S. military raid last month in Caracas that captured Venezuelan leader Nicolás Maduro, according to Reuters reporting carried by Al-Monitor.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/A7D453P21OS0siYas-4w7F_yzXLRM8GLyQ16yY60DyHdgjxha8rBgYbpE-2mxcVIELrpTFQg7b_JlnR8dZFgmxjAEumei1TQa2EzRFr_AaTiPSMZw14Kvi-5pNs_cIV1PN_NwshrVM7L1kBdpLJf2ybdZmvv6hqKVG0gnQxLpu850p2oVkYIj934qLSsbLZlGFn5AJkXhep36fNjSUWICz3V' alt='File photo illustrating U.S. actions targeting sanctioned oil shipments.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Tracking route: The Pentagon said U.S. forces tracked the tanker from Caribbean waters, then seized it in the Indian Ocean.</li><li>Sanctions basis: PBS said the Treasury Department’s website lists the tanker Bertha under U.S. sanctions related to Iran.</li><li>Interdiction count: SCMP called the boarding the 10th oil-tanker interdiction in the campaign.</li><li>Stated purpose: According to SCMP, the effort targets illicit oil tied to Venezuela.</li><li>Timing: Al Jazeera said the tanker was captured weeks after it reportedly left Venezuelan waters.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Department of Defense (Pentagon): The Pentagon said U.S. forces seized a sanctioned oil tanker in the Indian Ocean, the third interdiction in that region. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/us-forces-seize-third-sanctioned-oil-tanker-indian-ocean-pentagon-says'>Al-Monitor (via Reuters)</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said the United States has received 80 million barrels of Venezuelan oil, according to Al Jazeera’s report on the latest seizure. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/25/trump-says-us-has-received-80m-barrels-of-venezuelan-oil-3rd-tanker-seized'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Ship-tracking organization: A ship-movement tracking group cited by SCMP said the boarded vessel was the only tanker left to pursue after more than a dozen fled Venezuela’s coast. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3344520/us-boards-third-venezuela-linked-oil-tanker-indian-ocean'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3344520/us-boards-third-venezuela-linked-oil-tanker-indian-ocean'>US forces board third Venezuela-linked oil tanker in Indian Ocean</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/us-forces-seize-third-sanctioned-oil-tanker-indian-ocean-pentagon-says'>US forces seize third sanctioned oil tanker in Indian Ocean, Pentagon says</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-military-boards-third-sanctioned-oil-tanker-in-the-indian-ocean-after-tracking-it-from-the-caribbean'>U.S. military boards third sanctioned oil tanker in the Indian Ocean after tracking it from the Caribbean</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/25/trump-says-us-has-received-80m-barrels-of-venezuelan-oil-3rd-tanker-seized'>Trump says US has received 80m barrels of Venezuelan oil; 3rd tanker seized</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>